# This CITATION.cff describes how to cite the dagger *software*.
# Once the accompanying paper has an arXiv ID / JMLR entry, add a
# `preferred-citation` block here for the paper itself (see the CFF spec:
# https://github.com/citation-file-format/citation-file-format) rather than
# editing this file's `authors`/`title` to describe the paper in place.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "dagger: Diarization-guided, accumulation-free target speaker extraction"
abstract: >-
  Recovers one clean audio track per speaker from a single-channel recording
  where people talk over each other, using speaker diarization to enroll each
  speaker from their solo regions and an original TF-GridNet + cross-attention
  extractor to pull each speaker directly out of the original overlap
  mixture -- never from a subtracted residual -- so extraction error does not
  accumulate with overlap depth.
authors:
  - given-names: Rohan
    family-names: Banerjee
    alias: RohanBanerjee88
    email: banerj37@msu.edu
  - alias: AdityaAA2004
    email: anandad1@msu.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/RohanBanerjee88/dagger"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.0
keywords:
  - speech separation
  - target speaker extraction
  - speaker diarization
